A||N||29||rigdonhome||Fiero Philosophy, Hot Rod vs. Completely Stock||||10||
Z||000000||rigdonhome||08-25-2001||02:48 PM||||I bought a 35,000 mile, Cherry Fiero to do a V8 swap with...  I've received a lot of criticism for doing this to a Cherry Fiero!  <P>I look at it just like a '57 Chevy...  Some like to restore them to original condition, some like to Hot Rod them...  I prefer to make it FAST!  <P>Let me quote a friendly 'jab' from a fellow Fiero owner:<P>"next, don't you dare hack up that<BR>beautiful car!!! Honestly, I would garage that thing and buy a donor car to swap<BR>motors with, especially if you're going to stick with an automatic."<P>I guess I don't look at it as 'hacking up a beautiful car'...  I look at it as making it even better!  But again, that's personal preference...  I plan to keep all of the original parts so that the car could be put back in its original condition later if I want to...  I plan to keep this car forever.<P>My question is this:  "Will the V8 make my Fiero worth more or less money?"<P>Cheers,<BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.rigdonhome.com/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_driving_signature.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.rigdonhome.com/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_rear_signature.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.rigdonhome.com/cars/88_fiero_gt/rear_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Mach10||08-25-2001||02:57 PM||||More. A fiero's value is somewhat set, based on where you live and mileage etc. Putting in a new motor like that means that it's more of a custom job, and as such, you can sell it for whatever you'd like. You'd probably get it. HOWEVER, in terms of insurance, I don't believe you can insure it for much more withou purchasing some extra insurance, or having it re-registered as a "custom/kit" and not a "Pontiac Fiero"<P>It's your car, do what you want. <BR>||||reg||7
Z||000002||Galen||08-25-2001||03:23 PM||||whats a cherry fiero? <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">  Ray -    <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>    - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||08-25-2001||03:28 PM||||One that blushes at dirty jokes...||||reg||7
Z||000004||KissMySSFiero||08-25-2001||03:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>whats a cherry fiero? <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>a red one...<P><BR>i say invest in a nice small block.  <BR>pretty much everyone on the forum will tell you that the purple pavement eater is the nicest fiero around.  guess how many original miles it has.....under 25k according to the description on archies site.  <P>do your engine swap the way you want it.  i know i will.<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000005||rigdonhome||08-25-2001||03:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>whats a cherry fiero? <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry for the apparently not-so-well-known slang, 'Cherry'...<P>In my neck of the woods, 'Cherry' means in excellent condition, inside and out, in all aspects.  <P>'Cherry' has other meanings where I come from that I can't publish on a Family Forum like this...<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.rigdonhome.com/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_driving_signature.jpg[/IMG]<BR>[IMG]http://www.rigdonhome.com/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_rear_signature.jpg[/IMG]<BR>[IMG]http://www.rigdonhome.com/cars/88_fiero_gt/rear_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||rigdonhome||08-25-2001||03:55 PM||||Why in the heck can't I get my signature to show more than one picture???<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.rigdonhome.com/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_driving_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000007||maryjane||08-25-2001||03:56 PM||||Guess it depends how long you want to wait for the resale value to go up. A low mileage completly stock car in good cond will eventually be worth a lot, without much investment other than proper storage and routine maintenance. 'Course a car like the PPE or Skitime's is worth a LOT right now. (great job, Skitime, I drool thinkin about it.) Just depends what you want out of it and how quickly you want it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||rigdonhome||08-25-2001||03:59 PM||||I'm not at all looking at this car as an investment...  I'm more curious about its value than worried about it.  <P>I'm building it to have fun in, not to retire on!<P>Cheers,<BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_driving_signature.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/rear_signature.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_rear_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000009||Old Lar||08-25-2001||04:00 PM||||When you do major modifications, you limit the market for sales.  Unless the job is done professionally i.e. V8 Archie, and painted professionally, you have the hacked up Fiero conversion, pretty much worthless unless you find someone else who wants a hacked V8 Fiero swap.<P>So unless you are a professional at doing this project, the chances are you will have a worthless cherry Fiero with a V8 when your done.<P>So unless you have the big bucks to get it done right, I'd do a doner car for a first attempt rather than ruin a cherry Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000010||rigdonhome||08-25-2001||04:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Old Lar:<BR><B>When you do major modifications, you limit the market for sales.  Unless the job is done professionally i.e. V8 Archie, and painted professionally, you have the hacked up Fiero conversion, pretty much worthless unless you find someone else who wants a hacked V8 Fiero swap.<P>So unless you are a professional at doing this project, the chances are you will have a worthless cherry Fiero with a V8 when your done.<P>So unless you have the big bucks to get it done right, I'd do a doner car for a first attempt rather than ruin a cherry Fiero.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Believe it or not, there ARE people out there who are able to do a 'Professional' job with a conversion like this without paying big bucks for it.  In other words, I DO have more brains than money.<P>In fact, I find it impossible to find a 'Professional' that is capable of even doing a simple oil change to my satisfaction.  If you want it done right, you have to do it yourself.  (Sounds like Archie is an exception, but I doubt he does oil changes...)<P>I've been building Hot Rods for 15 years and have yet to end up with a 'hacked up' anything.  Even my trail truck (which LOOKS like absolute hell) looks like it came from the factory with the TPI V8 that I put in it.  It's a matter of craftsmanship and personal pride.  Check it out on my web site.<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_driving_signature.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/rear_signature.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_rear_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Mach10||08-25-2001||04:07 PM||||Old Lar: I would disagree with you on this. For the Pro/experienced Fiero owner, YES, it would be useless. <BR>However, you and I both know that market value is what people will pay for it. Over here, a hockey-puck-and-angle-iron v8 conversion would sell for over 9k CDN. I would offer the guy 4k. 1k less than the going rate for a decent v6 Fiero SE/GT.<P>Take my brother, for example. He paid 7k for an 88 Celica ALL-TRAC Turbo. Faster than hell, but in piss-poor condition. No brakes, leakey gas tank, oil leaks, split windsheild, no shocks/struts, rust. He could sell it in that same condition for 7k. Not because it's worth it, but because there will be someone dumb enough to repeat his mistake...<P>On a side note, he's FINALLY going to put that car in the condition it belongs in. He's planning to dump a few grand into restoring that thing. Good job, it's a nice car.||||reg||4
Z||000012||artherd||08-25-2001||04:12 PM||||Hiya Scott, these cars were made to be driven, and (in my opinion, in a perfect car-nut's world) to have v8 power!!!<P>Go for it, I can't *stand* this "garage the car and leave it there untill all it's rubber deteroirates, it's crank rusts, and it's tranny siezes crap!<P>Drive the car, drive it HARD, and *keep* it in tip-top shape!   Like you say below, it's a matter of personal pride and craftsmanship, and I'd like to add it's not a little bit of pure art :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000013||85fierogt||08-25-2001||05:45 PM||||personally i like to mod things out make it yours so to speak so i would do the engine swap, hell it your car you pay the insurance do what u wana do just dont crush it!<BR>peace<BR>-brad||||reg||6
Z||000014||Fierowrecker||08-25-2001||06:01 PM||||Hey Scott!<BR>It is YOUR car, do to it what makes YOU happy!!!<BR>Those other owners will drool over your conversion, as soon as it is done, and not say a word about having chopped up a cherry Fiero...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||KissMySSFiero||08-25-2001||06:07 PM||||when are you going to do it and what are you doin with the engine?   if you sell it and the price is right can i get first dibs?<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000016||AusFiero||08-25-2001||06:12 PM||||Yep do as you want with it. 35,000 miles is quite a lot really. Thats about 67,000 KMs which in this country isn't classified as low mileage. Now if it was 3500 then you would probably be losing out and destroyig a collectors item. Have fun in the V8. Or you could just forget the whole thing and ship over to me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000017||rigdonhome||08-25-2001||06:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KissMySSFiero:<BR><B>when are you going to do it and what are you doin with the engine?   if you sell it and the price is right can i get first dibs?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry, I plan to keep the engine for a couple of reasons...  1) If I ever want to restore it to original condition, I'll have all the parts.  2) It will look very cool on the engine stand in the garage!!!  If I do decide to sell it, though, I'll call you first!!!<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_driving_signature.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/rear_signature.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_rear_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Cooter||08-25-2001||06:38 PM||||Make it like you want it. If you decide to sell it later, you might have a hard time finding someone that appreciates it as much as you, but that is also true of that 57 Chevy. At work, we took a running/driving 47 Ford 4 door sedan with the original flathead v8- a somewhat rare car- and made a street rod with it. At first we caught some grief, but now everyone wants to go for a ride. Cars should be driven and enjoyed!||||reg||1
Z||000019||FieroBUZZ||08-25-2001||06:46 PM||||Scott:<BR>Have fun making and driving the car YOU want.  You can't satisfy everyone anyway. There are stock fans, mild hop-up guys and the wild ones......be a wild one!<BR>Gary<P>PS How will you drive it? From your sig you can't even reach the pedals.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000020||Cheever3000||08-25-2001||06:50 PM||||You asked for opinions.<BR>First, I do think the V8 would increase the value.  Just shop around.  Those for sale with V8's would barely have half the price tag with the stock engine.<BR>Second, I too would hate to see you do this to a "cherry" Fiero.  But I would not have said anything unless you asked my opinion.  And you did.  Maybe there's a voice inside you that says it's wrong, or you would not have asked.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000021||Cozmo||08-25-2001||07:21 PM||||<B>Hotrod it.</B><BR>There are enough decent Fieros around for the purists (flame suit on... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">).<BR>I do agree tho, if it was an '88 yellow T-top Formula or some other rare combo I would think twice about changing it from stock...<BR>The Fiero is the last of the true American customizable cars. <BR>Build what you imagine, and keep us updated on your adventure <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>BobC  ||||reg||14
Z||000022||Galen||08-25-2001||07:35 PM||||Sweet lookin car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>if I had a 88 Formula T-Top with a 5spd and no a/c..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'd drop the engine and slap a 3800 S/C in that sucker .. a nice 18/17in wheel combo(like that orange car <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) and be happy with myself<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">  Ray -    <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>    - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000023||Tigger||08-25-2001||07:49 PM||||     <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cooter:<BR><B>Cars should be driven and enjoyed!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Amen!<P>Don't worry about personalizing your Fiero, drop a V8 in it.  Done right it will increase it's value and make stock Fiero owners that much more jealous.<P>The only problem I see you'll run into is showing your car.  I've notice many Fiero shows break stock classes down by every year and make, then only have one custom and modified engine class.  Basically if you "think out of the box" just a bit, you get thrown into a class with 100% full show cars inside and out.  This is a real disadvantage for the "sleeper" car.  Also I see a lot of, best factory paint, best factory interior, best factory engine, etc. awards, however no awards for best custom in the same areas.  I've been to a few of these shows and it's disturbing to see a car win a couple "best factory" awards and also win their class while "hotrod" custom and modified owners kinda look at each other and wonder where they went wrong or if it was worth it to customize their Fieros.  I will say there are some shows that recognize this and break down the custom classes by number of modifications.<P>Really in the end, don't worry about what I just said, just build the car the way you like it and will make you the most happy.<P>BTW, I'm a "Hotrodder" too, I hacked up a beautiful '84 SE so much it's terrible.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue4.gif">     <BR>T-T-F-N, Ta Ta For Now!<BR><A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/tatooine/spielberg/241/" TARGET=_blank>Tigger's Fiero Page</A><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 08-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000024||Phil||08-25-2001||08:51 PM||||Hot rod it and drive it- I've put on 55,000 miles in the last 2 years<P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_1.gif">  <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
Z||000025||rigdonhome||08-25-2001||09:10 PM||||That's definitely my plan!!!<P>I LOVE to drive, especially a car as slick as a V8 Fiero!!!  <P>After I get my V8 swap done, I can show it off to the guys that garage theirs...  I can appreciate their opinion and desire to keep their cars stock, but it doesn't seem like they can appreciate the flip side.  Just my humble opinion...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_driving_signature.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/rear_signature.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_rear_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000026||CoolBlue87GT||08-25-2001||09:12 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KissMySSFiero:<BR><B><BR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR>whats a cherry fiero? <P>a red one...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Gee, can't a cherry one be Blue ?  LOL<P>I love seeing any type Fiero. As long as it's loved.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newcool1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 08-25-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000027||Tryxalon||08-25-2001||09:17 PM||||IF it is a well done custom job, good result, obvious pride and care in the detail;  any customization will add value to the item.  <P>But please do realize that when you make such a radical change as a non-stock engine to the car it is no longer a "fiero" it is, in reality, a "Hot Rod". It is a Custom Rod.  You know what the criteria is for such a custom made automobile to "shine" and win universal acclaim. If you can match that standard, go for it.  <P>I'm another who says that if you are capable of doing such work then you should do both.  Use a less than perfect Fiero and take it to that "Custom Hot Rod" level while maintaining a "cherry Fiero". That way you have the best of both worlds - Custom and Stock.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000028||FieroKyle||08-25-2001||09:45 PM||||These days there isn't much you can do to a Fiero to make it worth less. But are really worried about the value or bragging rights or a fun car to drive? Ask yourself this question first. See, I want a V8 Fiero really bad but I am afraid of getting one and feeling the guilt of may be even ruining a true American classic. But then I thin, whoa would those Vette guys really be shocked or that other kid in his 5.0 road  stain' (mustang haha) who hot rods all over town thinking he is the SH#T get a real eye opener when this Fiero kid shows him up. Also then I think, well there is always the local police problem where they search all over town to bust kids in their fast cars. But then again I think of totally restoring the car to 100% condition and showing it stock. I fight over myself with this question all the time.||||reg||2
Z||000029||DRH||08-25-2001||10:33 PM||||If you were doing this to a 10 mile, never been titled car I'd say you were nuts. A 38,000 mile car begs to be driven though. If you're going to put miles on it, I think the value of 'being original' diminishes quickly anyway.<P>I don't know about resale value, but it'll be a <B>long</B> time before anything but a never been titled car will have anywhere near the 'wow' value of a well done V8!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
